# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  PhantomSDR-Plus — phantomsdr-admin.service
#
#  Runs the admin panel under systemd instead of manage_admin.sh: it comes back
#  after a reboot and after a crash, on its own. Optional — manage_admin.sh is
#  perfectly fine if you are happy starting things by hand.
#
#  Install this one together with phantomsdr-proxy.service. The panel alone is
#  reachable only on localhost; the proxy is what puts it on your public port.
#
#  Why this matters for the thermal guard: the CPU over-temperature guard runs
#  INSIDE this process. No panel, no protection — which is exactly the situation
#  Restart=always and the boot-time start are here to prevent.
#
#  INSTALL
#    1. Edit User= and the two paths below to match your installation.
#    2. sudo cp phantomsdr-admin.service phantomsdr-proxy.service \
#              /etc/systemd/system/
#    3. sudo systemctl daemon-reload
#    4. ./manage_admin.sh stop        # free the ports first
#    5. sudo systemctl enable --now phantomsdr-admin
#       sudo systemctl enable --now phantomsdr-proxy
#    6. systemctl status phantomsdr-admin    # should say "active (running)"
#
#  AFTERWARDS, use systemctl — not manage_admin.sh — to stop or restart:
#
#    sudo systemctl restart phantomsdr-admin
#
#  'manage_admin.sh stop' is undone by systemd five seconds later, and
#  'manage_admin.sh restart' starts a second panel that races the one systemd
#  is about to start for the same port. 'manage_admin.sh status' stays useful.
#
#  To go back to the manual workflow:
#    sudo systemctl disable --now phantomsdr-admin
#    sudo systemctl disable --now phantomsdr-proxy
#
#
#  LOG OWNERSHIP — needed for the panel's "Clear Logs" button
#  systemd opens the StandardOutput=append: path from PID 1, before it drops to
#  User=, so a log that does not exist yet is created root:root 0644. The panel
#  runs as User= and then cannot truncate it: Clear Logs reports
#  "Permission denied: .../admin.log". Install tmpfiles/phantomsdr-logs.conf (edit
#  the paths and user first) so the log is re-created with the right owner at
#  every boot, and repair an existing one with
#  'sudo chown YOUR_USER:YOUR_GROUP admin.log' — chown, never rm: it is held open
#  O_APPEND. setup_admin.sh does both for you.
#
#  SupplementaryGroups=cpufreq gives the guard's throttle stage write access to
#  the CPU frequency ceiling without running the panel — and every start/stop
#  script it launches — as root. Create that group with ./setup-cpufreq-perms.sh
#  first, or systemd refuses to start the unit. Drop the line if you do not use
#  the throttle stage. systemd builds the group list fresh at every start, so
#  unlike an already-open login shell it needs no logout to pick the group up.
#
#  KillMode=process is load-bearing. The panel's Start button launches the
#  receiver as a child of this process, and a child inherits the unit's cgroup —
#  Python's start_new_session detaches the terminal and process group, but not
#  the cgroup. Under systemd's default KillMode=control-group, stopping the panel
#  would therefore SIGTERM and then SIGKILL spectrumserver, its watchdog and the
#  autorun daemon along with it, and stall the restart for the full 90 s stop
#  timeout. With =process systemd signals only the panel and leaves the rest of
#  the cgroup running, so restarting the panel no longer takes a busy receiver
#  off air. Do not remove the line without reading that paragraph twice.
#
#  FULL MANUAL: docs/THERMAL_GUARD.md · docs/ADMIN_PANEL_SETUP.md
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

[Unit]
Description=PhantomSDR Admin Panel
After=network.target

[Service]
Type=simple
User=YOUR_USER
SupplementaryGroups=cpufreq
WorkingDirectory=/home/YOUR_USER/PhantomSDR-Plus
ExecStart=/usr/bin/python3 -u /home/YOUR_USER/PhantomSDR-Plus/admin_server.py
StandardOutput=append:/home/YOUR_USER/PhantomSDR-Plus/admin.log
StandardError=append:/home/YOUR_USER/PhantomSDR-Plus/admin.log
KillMode=process
Restart=always
RestartSec=5

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
